 "preferred_name": "Reduction (complexity)",
 "kind": "method",
 "definition": "A way of converting one problem into another so that a solution to the second gives a solution to the first, used in complexity theory to compare how hard problems are.",
 "description": {
  "text": "In computability and complexity theory, an algorithm that transforms one problem into another. If problem A reduces to problem B efficiently, then B is at least as hard as A, because a solver for B could be used to solve A.",
